# PostgreSQL migration settings
# Copy this file to .env and replace both connection strings locally.
# Never commit .env or share its contents; .env is excluded by .gitignore.
#
# SOURCE_DATABASE_URL:
#   The existing Supabase PostgreSQL database to export from.
#   In Supabase, open Project Settings > Database > Connection string.
#   Choose URI and use the Direct connection or Session pooler URI.
#   Replace the password placeholder with the database password (not the
#   anon/publishable API key). URL-encode special characters in the password.
#   Add ?sslmode=require if it is not already included in the URI.
#
# DATABASE_URL:
#   The destination PostgreSQL database on this PC. PostgreSQL is expected
#   on 127.0.0.1:5432 and the destination database name is office_management.
#   Create the database before running a migration. Use the password you set
#   for your local PostgreSQL user, URL-encoding special characters.
#
# Do not run a migration until both connections are configured and verified.
# SOURCE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<encoded-password>@<supabase-db-host>:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<encoded-password>@127.0.0.1:5432/office_management
